        <div class="content lg-country-content"><h2> Netherlands Lottery Games </h2>
<p> Multiple Netherlands lotteries are available for daily opportunities to win significant sums of money. All national
  lottery games are owned and operated by Nederlandse Loterij. The Netherlands also participates in the popular
  Eurojackpot transnational game with 17 other countries. </p>
<h3> <a href="https://lotteryguru.com/netherlands-lottery-results/nl-eurojackpot"> Eurojackpot </a> </h3>
<p> Eurojackpot is a popular transnational lottery game that costs €2.00 to enter (in the Netherlands). </p>
<p> Players choose five numbers between 1 and 50 and two Euro Numbers between 1 and 10. Quick Picks are also available
  for random selections. </p>
<p> Participants can buy up to 50 tickets at a time for a single draw, with advance play also being available for the
  next five draws. Subscriptions can be taken out to ensure draws are never missed. </p>
<h3> Lucky Day </h3>
<p> Lucky Day is a Keno-style lottery game with multiple entry options. Stakes are available in increments of €1.50, up
  to a maximum of €22.50. </p>
<p> To enter, first choose how many numbers to bet on matching from one to 10. Next, choose the relevant number of
  selections from a pool of 1 to 80. </p>
<p> Players can enter up to 24 draws at a time, with subscriptions being available to ensure the draw is never missed.
</p>
<h3> <a href="https://lotteryguru.com/netherlands-lottery-results/nl-lotto"> Lotto </a> </h3>
<p> Lotto is the main lottery game in the Netherlands. Tickets cost €2.00. </p>
<p> Participants choose six numbers between 1 and 45, or can go for a Quick Pick for random selections. For an
  additional €1.00, players can add Lotto XL to their ticket to reutilize their chosen lottery numbers in a secondary
  draw, for the chance to win up to €1 million. </p>
<h3> State Lottery </h3>
<p> The Netherlands State Lottery is a raffle draw held 16 times a year. Entry costs a minimum of €3.50. </p>
<p> To enter, participants first buy a ticket printed with a random number. Tickets range from the 1/5 State Lottery,
  for a chance to win one fifth of each prize, to Boulevard for 100 full State Lottery tickets. Boulevard is a great way
  to increase the odds of winning, but costs €1,750! </p>
<h3> Million Dollar Game </h3>
<p> The Million Dollar Game is a unique lottery that costs €5.00 to enter. </p>
<p> Each ticket contains a random five-digit number and a letter of the alphabet. Players can change their chosen letter
  if they wish. </p>
<p> A colored ball is drawn at the start of each draw, with the €1 million jackpot only available if the green ball is
  drawn. If a purple ball is drawn, the starting jackpot of €10,000 is doubled. If any other color ball is drawn, the
  game has a fixed jackpot of €10,000. </p>
